  "notes": [
    "The outer contract stays Copilot-shaped: downstream apps still speak SDK JSON-RPC over ExternalServerConfig and do not need to learn Codex thread or turn verbs.",
    "The adapter module is split by responsibility: CLI boot policy in cli.py, subprocess/runtime transport in gateway.py, orchestration and event routing in server.py, and pure translation or policy logic in mappers.py plus tool_policy.py.",
    "Session continuity is adapter-owned state. session_store.py persists SDK session id to Codex thread id together with cwd, model, and tool fingerprint so incompatible resume fails early instead of drifting at runtime.",
    "Proof is part of the module story, not an afterthought. Fake-gateway parity tests lock observable behavior, and the live smoke script proves the packaged CLI can drive a real codex app-server without touching reserved ports 4800, 4801, or 4811."
  ]
